In Python file handling, the open() function has several modes. The most important ones are r, w, a, and x.

Main file modes
Mode	Name	What it does
"r"	Read	Reads an existing file
"w"	Write	Writes to a file; overwrites existing content
"a"	Append	Adds content to the end of the file
"x"	Create	Creates a new file; error if it already exists
Read + Write combinations
Mode	Meaning
"r+"	Read + write; file must already exist
"w+"	Read + write; overwrites the file
"a+"	Read + append; creates file if it doesn't exist